{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"EXT_ID:15692043 AND SRC:MED","internalQuery":"EXT_ID:15692043 AND SRC:MED","resultType":"CORE","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"15692043","source":"MED","pmid":"15692043","doi":"10.1126/science.1104607","title":"Crystal structure of a complex between the catalytic and regulatory (RIalpha) subunits of PKA.","authorString":"Kim C, Xuong NH, Taylor SS.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Kim C","lastName":"Kim","firstName":"Choel","initials":"C","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry, University of California, San Diego, CA 92093, USA."}]}},{"fullName":"Xuong NH","lastName":"Xuong","firstName":"Nguyen-Huu","initials":"NH"},{"fullName":"Taylor SS","lastName":"Taylor","firstName":"Susan S","initials":"SS"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics","recommended_reviews","related_data","wikipedia"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"5710","volume":"307","journalIssueId":1218206,"dateOfPublication":"2005 Feb","monthOfPublication":2,"yearOfPublication":2005,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Science","title":"Science (New York, N.Y.)","essn":"1095-9203","issn":"0036-8075","nlmid":"0404511","isoabbreviation":"Science"},"printPublicationDate":"2005-02-01"},"pubYear":"2005","pageInfo":"690-696","abstractText":"The 2.0-angstrom structure of the cyclic adenosine monophosphate (cAMP)-dependent protein kinase (PKA) catalytic subunit bound to a deletion mutant of a regulatory subunit (RIalpha) defines a previously unidentified extended interface. The complex provides a molecular mechanism for inhibition of PKA and suggests how cAMP binding leads to activation. The interface defines the large lobe of the catalytic subunit as a stable scaffold where Tyr247 in the G helix and Trp196 in the phosphorylated activation loop serve as anchor points for binding RIalpha. These residues compete with cAMP for the phosphate binding cassette in RIalpha. In contrast to the catalytic subunit, RIalpha undergoes major conformational changes when the complex is compared with cAMP-bound RIalpha. The inhibitor sequence docks to the active site, whereas the linker, also disordered in free RIalpha, folds across the extended interface. The beta barrel of cAMP binding domain A, which is the docking site for cAMP, remains largely intact in the complex, whereas the helical subdomain undergoes major reorganization.","affiliation":"Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry, University of California, San Diego, CA 92093, USA.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Research Support, U.S. Gov't, P.H.S.","Research Support, U.S. Gov't, Non-P.H.S.","Journal Article"]},"grantsList":{"grant":[{"agency":"NIDDK NIH HHS","acronym":"DK","grantId":"DK07233","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NIGMS NIH HHS","acronym":"GM","grantId":"GM19301","orderIn":0},{"agency":"NIGMS NIH HHS","acronym":"GM","grantId":"GM34921","orderIn":0}]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Cyclic AMP-Dependent Protein Kinases","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"AI","qualifierName":"antagonists & inhibitors"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"CH","qualifierName":"chemistry"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Tryptophan","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"CH","qualifierName":"chemistry"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Tyrosine","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"CH","qualifierName":"chemistry"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Cyclic AMP","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"ME","qualifierName":"metabolism"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Crystallization"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptor